problemStatement:
Consider the following version of **Bubble Sort**:

```
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < n - 1; j++) {
        if (a[j] > a[j + 1]) {
            swap(a[j], a[j + 1]);
        }
    }
}
```

Given an array `a`, determine the **total number of swaps** that occur while sorting it with this algorithm.

